=== REASONING ===
Phase 38-08 is a decision record (no source edits) that fixes the scope, defaults,
and safety contract for extending api_call_logs coverage in the implementation
prompts that follow (Prompts 09-13). The decisions captured here are:

(1) SCOPE EXPANSION
    This phase declares that subsequent prompts will add two new DB sinks to
    api_call_logs:
      - INBOUND sink: a chi middleware that records every /api/v1/* request
        the API server handles, with one row per request, tagged service="api-inbound".
      - OUTBOUND sink: a shared *http.Client RoundTripper used by all outbound
        adapters (geocoders, EIA, GitHub releases, notification webhooks, Tesla
        auth/refresh, and worker-originated calls). Per-adapter service tags such
        as "geocoder-nominatim", "geocoder-google", "geocoder-azure", "gas-prices-eia",
        "github-releases", "notify-discord", "notify-slack", "notify-ntfy",
        "notify-pushover", "notify-webhook", "tesla-auth", "automation-worker",
        and "notification-worker" will be used so the existing
        web/src/features/admin/pages/ApiLogsPage.tsx stats.by_service tile and
        Badge SERVICE_CONFIG remain the source of truth for the UI.

(2) NO SCHEMA CHANGE
    No new schema in this phase. The api_call_logs hypertable, its 7-day chunks,
    30-day compression policy, and 365-day retention policy are unchanged.
    The existing service column (added in 000009) and req_body/resp_body columns
    (added in 000149) are sufficient for the new sinks. This phase introduces
    no migrations.

(3) BODY CAPTURE DEFAULT
    Body capture defaults to OFF. It is gated behind the API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES
    env var (operator must opt in). Even when ON, bodies are clipped to a hard
    maximum size, and JSON bodies are walked to redact any field whose key
    matches the redaction list before persistence. Operator default for this
    decision record is recorded below as BODY_CAPTURE_DEFAULT.

(4) ASYNC BATCHED WRITER (latency safety)
    All inserts MUST go through an async batched writer. The request path
    (inbound middleware) and outbound RoundTripper enqueue records into a
    bounded in-memory channel; a background goroutine drains and INSERTs in
    batches. If the channel is full the record is DROPPED with a counter
    increment (zerolog warn + Prometheus counter) - api_call_logs MUST NOT
    block, slow, or fail any user-facing request or outbound adapter call.
    This is the single most important latency contract for this expansion.

(5) REDACTION (privacy + secret hygiene)
    Always redact:
      - The Authorization request header (replace with "REDACTED").
      - Any header, query parameter, JSON body field, or form field whose
        case-insensitive name contains: key, token, secret, password, cookie.
      - Cookie response headers and Set-Cookie response headers.
    Redaction runs BEFORE the record is enqueued so secrets never sit in the
    in-memory channel even briefly. Tesla VINs and access tokens MUST be
    redacted under this rule (they match key/token).

(6) PATH SKIP-LIST (avoid feedback loops and noise)
    The inbound middleware MUST skip these paths so api_call_logs cannot
    self-amplify or drown in trivial traffic:
      - /healthz
      - /readyz
      - /metrics
      - /api/v1/system/status
      - /api/v1/system/audit
      - /api/v1/events*       (all SSE endpoints)
      - /api/v1/sse-token
      - the api-logs admin endpoints themselves (whatever the system/audit
        sub-router exposes for reading/exporting api_call_logs).
    Skipping the api-logs admin endpoints prevents the obvious feedback loop
    where opening the /api-logs page generates more rows than it displays.

(7) BARE CLIENT MIGRATION
    Prompt 13 will migrate bare *http.Client / http.DefaultClient usages in
    internal/geocoding, internal/integrations, internal/notifications,
    internal/tesla auth/refresh paths, and the worker packages over to the
    shared instrumented client constructed via the new RoundTripper. The
    existing teslaClient.SetLogCallback hook in cmd/teslasync/main.go:160 is
    PRESERVED for backward compatibility but its records will continue to be
    tagged service="tesla-api" exactly as today; we will not double-log.

CONTRACT SUMMARY (one line each, for the gate regex):
  - writes are async batched (non-blocking, bounded channel, drop-on-full).
  - the writer must redact Authorization plus key/token/secret/password/cookie fields.
  - this phase has no new schema; api_call_logs schema is unchanged.

